@title Cold Room B temperature alarm
@subtitle Marlowe Vaccine Depot runbook, owned by Depot Operations
@author Depot Operations, Owner

kpi Safe range | 2 to 8 °C | Cold Room B, 12400 doses | neutral
kpi Warning | > 8 °C | for 10 minutes | neutral
kpi Critical | > 12 °C or < 0 °C | act at once | bad
kpi Night supervisor | 555-0187 | Gabriela Nunez | neutral

!!! NEVER DISCARD ANY DOSES. Nobody throws anything away, whatever the temperature reading. Only the Quality Manager decides what is discarded.

## Alarm levels

table = level,trigger; Warning,Above 8 °C for 10 minutes; Critical,Above 12 °C or below 0 °C

## First 15 minutes

1. Acknowledge the alarm on the monitoring panel within 5 minutes.
2. Check that the door is fully shut and the seal is intact.
3. Check that the compressor has power and note the temperature shown on the data logger.
4. Call the refrigeration contractor Polar Service on 555-0190. They respond within 4 hours.

## Moving stock

If the temperature is still above 8 °C after 15 minutes, move the doses.

- Move up to 9000 doses to backup Cold Room C.
- Put the remaining 3400 doses into the 6 validated transport boxes with ice packs.
- Log every box on the transfer sheet.

## Quarantine and escalation

- Any lot out of range for more than 30 minutes in total is quarantined. Tell the Quality Manager immediately.
- If the alarm is not resolved within 2 hours, call the Operations Director.

!!! Do not discard anything. Quarantined lots stay in quarantine until the Quality Manager decides.

